  "articleHtml": "<main>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Biscuitville Nutrition Calculator\n    </span>\n</p>\n<div>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n      Meta Title:\n     </span>\n<span>\n      Biscuitville Nutrition Calculator: Calories &amp; Macros\n     </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n      Meta Description:\n     </span>\n<span>\n      Check Biscuitville calories, protein, carbs, fat, sodium, and nutrition facts for biscuits, breakfast platters, sides, drinks, sauces, and more.\n     </span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.dy55mg7tna9v\">\n<span>\n     Biscuitville Nutrition Calculator\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Biscuitville meals are built around more than the biscuit itself. Eggs, bacon, sausage, country ham, fried chicken, cheese, hashbrowns, grits, gravy, sauces, and drinks can all change the nutrition of your final breakfast.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Use the\n    </span>\n<span>\n     Biscuitville Nutrition Calculator above\n    </span>\n<span>\n     to compare menu items and build the nutrition for the breakfast you actually order.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.ykfi5o54ro3d\">\n<span>\n     Start With the Biscuit Filling\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Two Biscuitville sandwiches can use the same scratch-made biscuit but still have very different calories and macros.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     A plain biscuit on the current NutritionSolver menu has\n    </span>\n<span>\n     260 calories\n    </span>\n<span>\n     , while fillings such as sausage, fried chicken, egg, cheese, or country ham add different amounts of protein, fat, and sodium.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     That makes the filling just as important as the biscuit when comparing breakfast choices.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     For example, the current database lists:\n    </span>\n</p>\n<ul class=\"space-y-2 mb-6 ml-4 list-disc list-inside text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base\">\n<li class=\"leading-relaxed text-zinc-300\">\n<span>\n      Bacon, Egg &amp; Cheese Biscuit: 440 calories\n     </span>\n</li>\n<li class=\"leading-relaxed text-zinc-300\">\n<span>\n      Fried Chicken Biscuit: 470 calories\n     </span>\n</li>\n<li class=\"leading-relaxed text-zinc-300\">\n<span>\n      Sausage &amp; Egg Biscuit: 480 calories\n     </span>\n</li>\n<li class=\"leading-relaxed text-zinc-300\">\n<span>\n      Fried Steak Biscuit: 580 calories\n     </span>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Compare the complete sandwich rather than assuming every biscuit-based item has a similar nutrition profile.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.nlnxxi16gkzj\">\n<span>\n     Breakfast Platters Need to Be Calculated as a Meal\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Biscuitville also serves breakfast platters that can combine eggs, meat, a biscuit, and a side such as grits or hashbrowns. Its official menu currently includes both standard breakfast platters and larger BVL Ultimate Breakfast Platters.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     For these meals, checking only the meat or eggs will underestimate the full order.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Add each available component to the meal builder so you can see the combined:\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Calories\n     <br/>\n     Protein\n     <br/>\n     Carbohydrates\n     <br/>\n     Fat\n     <br/>\n     Sodium\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     This gives you a more useful picture of the plate as a whole.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.y1wjkdn1oeo7\">\n<span>\n     Sodium Can Change Quickly Between Biscuit Choices\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Calories do not tell the entire story at breakfast.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Several Biscuitville sandwiches in the current database contain more than 1,000mg of sodium. For example, the Country Ham Biscuit is listed at\n    </span>\n<span>\n     1,270mg\n    </span>\n<span>\n     , while the Sausage Gravy Biscuit is listed at\n    </span>\n<span>\n     1,480mg\n    </span>\n<span>\n     .\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     This is why it is worth comparing sodium separately when choosing between biscuits with similar calorie totals.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Meats, cheese, gravy, sauces, and seasoned sides can all contribute to the final sodium amount.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.afjdna5zypzd\">\n<span>\n     Bigger Biscuits Can Change More Than Portion Size\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Biscuitville's\n    </span>\n<span>\n     BVL Ultimate\n    </span>\n<span>\n     line uses larger combinations, such as extra meat and cheese. The current official menu describes the Ultimate lineup as offering double meat and double cheese on selected biscuits.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Larger portions can increase protein, but they may also increase calories, fat, saturated fat, and sodium.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     If you are deciding between a regular biscuit and an Ultimate version, compare the full nutrition profile rather than looking only at the extra protein.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.qzvarnqfjvrj\">\n<span>\n     Sides and Sauces Belong in the Calculation\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Hashbrowns, grits, sausage gravy, country fries, cheese grits, ranch, honey mustard, and other extras are separate parts of the meal.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Biscuitville's current menu includes both classic and premium sides, along with multiple sauces and condiments.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     If you add a side or dipping sauce, include it in the meal builder. Otherwise, the total shown for the main biscuit will not represent the complete breakfast.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.i61udmdzrvzp\">\n<span>\n     Biscuitville Nutrition Questions\n    </span>\n</h2><div class=\"faq-accordion-container space-y-3 my-6\"><details class=\"faq-accordion-item glass-card-static rounded-xl border border-zinc-800/80 p-0 mb-3 overflow-hidden group\"><summary class=\"faq-accordion-summary font-bold text-white text-sm md:text-base cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between p-4 bg-zinc-900/60 hover:bg-zinc-900 transition-colors\"><span>How many calories are in a Biscuitville biscuit?</span><span>+</span></summary><div class=\"faq-accordion-answer p-4 text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/40\"></div></details><details class=\"faq-accordion-item glass-card-static rounded-xl border border-zinc-800/80 p-0 mb-3 overflow-hidden group\"><summary class=\"faq-accordion-summary font-bold text-white text-sm md:text-base cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between p-4 bg-zinc-900/60 hover:bg-zinc-900 transition-colors\"><span>Which Biscuitville biscuits have more protein?</span><span>+</span></summary><div class=\"faq-accordion-answer p-4 text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/40\"></div></details><details class=\"faq-accordion-item glass-card-static rounded-xl border border-zinc-800/80 p-0 mb-3 overflow-hidden group\"><summary class=\"faq-accordion-summary font-bold text-white text-sm md:text-base cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between p-4 bg-zinc-900/60 hover:bg-zinc-900 transition-colors\"><span>Do Biscuitville sides count separately?</span><span>+</span></summary><div class=\"faq-accordion-answer p-4 text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/40\"></div></details><details class=\"faq-accordion-item glass-card-static rounded-xl border border-zinc-800/80 p-0 mb-3 overflow-hidden group\"><summary class=\"faq-accordion-summary font-bold text-white text-sm md:text-base cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between p-4 bg-zinc-900/60 hover:bg-zinc-900 transition-colors\"><span>Why can Biscuitville menu nutrition change?</span><span>+</span></summary><div class=\"faq-accordion-answer p-4 text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/40\"></div></details></div>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.6j444zb1m5j\">\n<span>\n     About the Biscuitville Nutrition Data\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     NutritionSolver organizes available\n    </span>\n<span>\n     Biscuitville nutrition information\n    </span>\n<span>\n     across biscuits, breakfast platters, English muffins, sides, drinks, condiments, and other menu categories.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Use the calculator to compare individual foods or combine multiple items into one breakfast total. Restaurant nutrition values represent standard menu information and may vary slightly with preparation, substitutions, and menu updates.\n    </span>\n</p>\n</main>",
  "seoTitle": "Biscuitville Nutrition Calculator: Calories & Macros",
  "seoDescription": "Check Biscuitville calories, protein, carbs, fat, sodium, and nutrition facts for biscuits, breakfast platters, sides, drinks, sauces, and more.",
  "faqs": [
    {
      "q": "How many calories are in a Biscuitville biscuit?",
      "a": "It depends on the biscuit and filling. The current database lists a plain biscuit at about\n    \n\n     260 calories\n    \n\n     , while meat, egg, cheese, gravy, and larger portions can raise the total considerably."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which Biscuitville biscuits have more protein?",
      "a": "Biscuits containing chicken, sausage, eggs, ham, or larger meat portions generally provide more protein than a plain or cheese-only biscuit. Use the protein values in the calculator to compare exact items."
    },
    {
      "q": "Do Biscuitville sides count separately?",
      "a": "Yes. Hashbrowns, grits, gravy, fries, and other sides have their own nutrition values and should be added separately when calculating a full meal."
    },
    {
      "q": "Why can Biscuitville menu nutrition change?",
      "a": "Seasonal products, new menu items, portion changes, and recipe updates can change the nutrition data over time. Biscuitville's current ordering menu, for example, includes seasonal items alongside its regular biscuits and platters."
    }
  ]
}